  "has_quantitative_results": true,
  "summary": "The paper proposes CL-QAS, a continual-learning quantum architecture search framework using tensor-train amplitude encoding and reinforcement-learning-driven circuit design. Experiments with 20‑qubit, 6‑layer VQCs on ECG classification and synthetic financial forecasting show improvements over baseline VQCs, e.g., ECG F1 score 0.819 vs 0.741 (Naive‑VQC) in noiseless simulation and hardware accuracy 0.863 ± 0.008 on IBM Heron r2. Results demonstrate improved robustness and continual learning performance but do not establish quantum advantage over classical methods.",
